## What I did

**Census first.** The open unit was **T-785** — reopened at 07:39Z with no work done, last AC blocked on T-353's human ruling. Parked back through the verb.

**Unit 1 — T-826** (Q1, hv-lc, BVP 115). Verifying its ACs before building found five of eight already delivered under *other* task ids, and AC 5 pointing at a live red: T-875's two `kind` validator rules had **never been seen to fire**, one was unclassified in the anchorability table, and the other was `PAIRED` in the parity table but absent from the cross-form harness's `PAIRS` — so "the two forms agree on kind" was a claim no comparison had made. Closed rule-scoped: two persistent fixtures, a new `DOC-META` anchor class that **refuses a green that was available** (declaring it `NODE` would have passed and lied), and the bridge's erasure of `workflowMeta` named rather than absorbed as a repair. Teeth 15/15, verify 8/8. Parked at `issues` — AC 4 is T-876 (held by PD-343) and AC 6 contradicts T-213's ratified disposition, which I did not rewrite.

**Unit 2 — T-573** (Q1, hv-lc, cost 1.9). **Closed.** The Emits panel wrote a string where the exporter required an array, so the ratified shape was unreachable from the panel. Fixed with one module-scope vocabulary and a content-equality guard. 8/8 CDP legs (with a pre-fix control arm), 5/5 mutants, 24/24 byte-identity, two screenshots read, RCA captured — G-019 refused the close for an empty RCA and was right to.

## Worth your attention

- **The board is decision-limited, not capacity-limited.** I stopped at 385K of an 800K budget: Q1 is empty and all four eligible Q2 tasks are Sovereign-blocked. Six of seven questions have been open across all three rounds. Unblocking any one of **T-353**, **T-889 AC 1**, or **T-358's five-way `[REVIEW]`** converts a high-value task into a single round's work.
- **Filed and scored:** T-925 (142 — the bridge erases document-level `workflowMeta`; Sovereign at step 1), T-926, T-927, T-928, T-929, T-930, plus OBS-440/441/445/446/447.
- **Two corrections to my own findings are in the record, not deleted:** T-341 is not a phantom (T-891 says so in its own description), and OBS-441's diagnosis was wrong — root cause is T-929.
- **§12, found in the final check:** a concurrent session worked this worktree all round, closed T-785 35 minutes after I parked it, and is working T-669. That resolves the focus-drift finding — `focus.yaml` is session-global with no ownership check — and it means I ran a selection pass against a register another process was mutating. That one's on me; the dispatch note warned me to re-read `git log`, and I read it at the start and not again until the end.

No `--force`, `--skip-*`, or bypass of any kind. Six commits, all local and unpushed (`fw handover` still pushes to origin without a flag — OBS-413).
